# Drafted by Gemini (R21 booths2), edited.

~ e_start
fd_host_strongarm [smile]: Step right up to the pine plank, little bones. Put your elbow down and show the Horned Bear what grit you kept.
if not ((flag.revelers_freed == 0 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 0) or (flag.revelers_freed == 1 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 1) or (flag.revelers_freed == 2 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 2) or (flag.revelers_freed == 3 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 3) or (flag.revelers_freed == 4 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 4) or (flag.revelers_freed == 5 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 5) or (flag.revelers_freed == 6 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 6) or (flag.revelers_freed == 7 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 7) or (flag.revelers_freed == 8 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 8) or (flag.revelers_freed == 9 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 9) or (flag.revelers_freed == 10 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 10) or (flag.revelers_freed == 11 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 11) or (flag.revelers_freed == 12 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 12))
fd_host_strongarm [sly]: You have had your turn at the timber, friends. Come back when the festival air shifts and something has changed.
endif
* [if ((flag.revelers_freed == 0 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 0) or (flag.revelers_freed == 1 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 1) or (flag.revelers_freed == 2 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 2) or (flag.revelers_freed == 3 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 3) or (flag.revelers_freed == 4 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 4) or (flag.revelers_freed == 5 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 5) or (flag.revelers_freed == 6 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 6) or (flag.revelers_freed == 7 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 7) or (flag.revelers_freed == 8 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 8) or (flag.revelers_freed == 9 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 9) or (flag.revelers_freed == 10 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 10) or (flag.revelers_freed == 11 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 11) or (flag.revelers_freed == 12 and flag.booth_e_plays <= 12))] Play a round -> e_play
* Ask how the game works -> e_rules
* Look around the booth -> e_notice
* Challenge the worker -> e_fight
* Walk on -> END

~ e_rules
fd_host_strongarm [neutral]: Plant your elbow in the notch, clasp the hairy paw, and press until knuckles kiss the wood. Small mercy wins one ticket, true might takes ten.
-> e_start

~ e_notice
Narrator: Behind a rack of dried antlers and tallow ribbons, a villager sewn into a clumsy bear pelt sways in time to the pipes, grinning through painted wooden teeth.
set found_bear
-> e_start

~ e_fight
fd_host_strongarm [smile]: Oh, a free-for-all is grand sport too. Mind the splinters when the table goes over.
Narrator: The bear host never drops that wide carnival grin, even as he squares his shoulders; strike him down and another pair of hands will staff the plank before the sawdust settles.
combat booth_e

~ e_play
if flag.revelers_freed == 0
set booth_e_plays = 1
elif flag.revelers_freed == 1
set booth_e_plays = 2
elif flag.revelers_freed == 2
set booth_e_plays = 3
elif flag.revelers_freed == 3
set booth_e_plays = 4
elif flag.revelers_freed == 4
set booth_e_plays = 5
elif flag.revelers_freed == 5
set booth_e_plays = 6
elif flag.revelers_freed == 6
set booth_e_plays = 7
elif flag.revelers_freed == 7
set booth_e_plays = 8
elif flag.revelers_freed == 8
set booth_e_plays = 9
elif flag.revelers_freed == 9
set booth_e_plays = 10
elif flag.revelers_freed == 10
set booth_e_plays = 11
elif flag.revelers_freed == 11
set booth_e_plays = 12
elif flag.revelers_freed == 12
set booth_e_plays = 13
endif
set found_bear
Narrator: The plank smells of old mutton fat and pine resin. Across it, the host sets a massive scarred forearm down with a dull thud that rattles the bone charms on his coat.
* [Athletics DC 20] Arm wrestle for one ticket -> e_win | e_lose
* [Athletics DC 25] Go for the big wrestle for ten tickets -> e_big | e_lose
* [Intimidation DC 15] Stare the bear down -> e_win | e_lose
* [Deception DC 15] Slip in a trick elbow -> e_win | e_lose
* Back away -> END

~ e_win
set fool_tickets += 1
fd_host_strongarm [smile]: Down goes the paw, fair enough for carnival work. Take your ticket before the grease cools.
-> e_start

~ e_big
set fool_tickets += 10
fd_host_strongarm [weary]: By the old horns, you cracked the grain right down the middle of my good oak board. Take the whole ribbon of ten before you tear my shoulder out of its stitching.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Fine leverage, friends, though I pity the joinery on that table.
-> e_start

~ e_lose
Narrator: Your arm trembles against a limb like seasoned bog oak, and the table does not budge a hair.
fd_host_strongarm [sly]: Still as a headstone, little mortal. Shake out your wrist and try again when the music changes.
-> e_start

~ f_start
fd_host_drink [smile]: Mind the skirts and mind the shingles, darlings, there is always a fresh kettle steeping under the eaves. Step up and wet your whistle.
if not ((flag.revelers_freed == 0 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 0) or (flag.revelers_freed == 1 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 1) or (flag.revelers_freed == 2 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 2) or (flag.revelers_freed == 3 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 3) or (flag.revelers_freed == 4 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 4) or (flag.revelers_freed == 5 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 5) or (flag.revelers_freed == 6 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 6) or (flag.revelers_freed == 7 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 7) or (flag.revelers_freed == 8 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 8) or (flag.revelers_freed == 9 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 9) or (flag.revelers_freed == 10 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 10) or (flag.revelers_freed == 11 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 11) or (flag.revelers_freed == 12 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 12))
fd_host_drink [weary]: Now, now, you have had your sip from the cellar already. Come back when something in the square has changed.
endif
* [if ((flag.revelers_freed == 0 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 0) or (flag.revelers_freed == 1 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 1) or (flag.revelers_freed == 2 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 2) or (flag.revelers_freed == 3 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 3) or (flag.revelers_freed == 4 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 4) or (flag.revelers_freed == 5 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 5) or (flag.revelers_freed == 6 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 6) or (flag.revelers_freed == 7 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 7) or (flag.revelers_freed == 8 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 8) or (flag.revelers_freed == 9 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 9) or (flag.revelers_freed == 10 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 10) or (flag.revelers_freed == 11 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 11) or (flag.revelers_freed == 12 and flag.booth_f_plays <= 12))] Play a round -> f_play
* Ask how the game works -> f_rules
* Look around the booth -> f_notice
* Challenge the worker -> f_fight
* Walk on -> END

~ f_rules
fd_host_drink [sly]: One tin cup of house cordial at a time, sweethearts. Keep it down with a smile and two tickets are yours, though three cups will turn a stout stomach inside out.
-> f_start

~ f_notice
Narrator: Half-hidden behind the painted dollhouse counter, a townsfolk trapped inside a teetering wicker manor on yellow chicken legs hops from foot to foot, humming merrily.
set found_hut
-> f_start

~ f_fight
fd_host_drink [smile]: Spilling the punch already, are we? Do be careful not to tread on my good crockery.
Narrator: Her painted smile never wavers as she reaches beneath the counter; even if you smash this booth to kindling, another smiling host will pour the next round before anyone notices.
combat booth_f

~ f_play
if flag.revelers_freed == 0
set booth_f_plays = 1
elif flag.revelers_freed == 1
set booth_f_plays = 2
elif flag.revelers_freed == 2
set booth_f_plays = 3
elif flag.revelers_freed == 3
set booth_f_plays = 4
elif flag.revelers_freed == 4
set booth_f_plays = 5
elif flag.revelers_freed == 5
set booth_f_plays = 6
elif flag.revelers_freed == 6
set booth_f_plays = 7
elif flag.revelers_freed == 7
set booth_f_plays = 8
elif flag.revelers_freed == 8
set booth_f_plays = 9
elif flag.revelers_freed == 9
set booth_f_plays = 10
elif flag.revelers_freed == 10
set booth_f_plays = 11
elif flag.revelers_freed == 11
set booth_f_plays = 12
elif flag.revelers_freed == 12
set booth_f_plays = 13
endif
set found_hut
set fd_drinks = 0
-> f_cup

~ f_cup
Narrator: She ladles out a dented tin cup of thick, greenish liquor that smells of pond weeds, burnt sugar, and cellar damp.
* [Constitution DC 12] Down the cup -> f_ok | f_bad
* [Sleight of Hand DC 14] Pour it into a plant pot when the hostess looks away -> f_ok | f_bad
* Decline -> f_start

~ f_ok
set fool_tickets += 2
set fd_drinks += 1
if flag.fd_drinks >= 3
-> f_sick
endif
fd_host_drink [smile]: Down the hatch and not a drop wasted on your collar. Here are two tickets, thirsty lamb, unless you fancy another ladle.
* Another cup -> f_cup
* Enough -> f_start

~ f_bad
damage 1d4 poison
Narrator: Your throat clenches around the rank, oily brew, and your eyes water as a sour heat curdles in your belly.
fd_host_drink [sly]: Oh dear, that is the face of someone chewing on a toad. Best wipe your chin and step back from the kettle.
-> f_start

~ f_sick
damage 1d6 poison
disadvantage checks 1h: the cups
Narrator: A third measure is more than flesh was made to hold; the carnival lanterns spin in greasy circles as your stomach heaves.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Your stomach is rejecting that pond-weed almost to the second. Remarkable.
fd_host_drink [smile]: Three cups deep and green around the gills, just as promised. Take your tickets and go lean against a fence post, darling.
-> f_start

~ g_start
fd_host_puppets [smile]: Draw near the velvet curtain, heroes of the hour. Every grand deed deserves a second life in painted wood and bright red ribbon.
if not ((flag.revelers_freed == 0 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 0) or (flag.revelers_freed == 1 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 1) or (flag.revelers_freed == 2 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 2) or (flag.revelers_freed == 3 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 3) or (flag.revelers_freed == 4 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 4) or (flag.revelers_freed == 5 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 5) or (flag.revelers_freed == 6 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 6) or (flag.revelers_freed == 7 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 7) or (flag.revelers_freed == 8 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 8) or (flag.revelers_freed == 9 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 9) or (flag.revelers_freed == 10 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 10) or (flag.revelers_freed == 11 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 11) or (flag.revelers_freed == 12 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 12))
fd_host_puppets [neutral]: The curtain is drawn on your act for now, my friends. Return when something out on the cobbles has changed.
endif
* [if ((flag.revelers_freed == 0 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 0) or (flag.revelers_freed == 1 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 1) or (flag.revelers_freed == 2 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 2) or (flag.revelers_freed == 3 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 3) or (flag.revelers_freed == 4 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 4) or (flag.revelers_freed == 5 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 5) or (flag.revelers_freed == 6 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 6) or (flag.revelers_freed == 7 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 7) or (flag.revelers_freed == 8 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 8) or (flag.revelers_freed == 9 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 9) or (flag.revelers_freed == 10 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 10) or (flag.revelers_freed == 11 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 11) or (flag.revelers_freed == 12 and flag.booth_g_plays <= 12))] Play a round -> g_play
* Ask how the game works -> g_rules
* Look around the booth -> g_notice
* Challenge the worker -> g_fight
* Walk on -> END

~ g_rules
fd_host_puppets [sly]: Watch my little darlings act out your finest triumph. Spot the stagecraft in the strings or give the play a true line from your own mouth, and three tickets are yours.
-> g_start

~ g_notice
Narrator: Just beside the puppet booth's striped valance, a dazed villager laced into the stiff motley of Chuckles's flag-bearer waves a tattered pennant in endless figure-eights.
set found_flag
-> g_start

~ g_fight
fd_host_puppets [smile]: Ah, the audience storms the stage. Mind the wires, they tangle terribly round the throat.
Narrator: The puppeteer beams without a flicker of fear as his wooden fingers clack together; break him if you must, for another smiling player will take up the strings before the crowd blinks.
combat booth_g

~ g_play
if flag.revelers_freed == 0
set booth_g_plays = 1
elif flag.revelers_freed == 1
set booth_g_plays = 2
elif flag.revelers_freed == 2
set booth_g_plays = 3
elif flag.revelers_freed == 3
set booth_g_plays = 4
elif flag.revelers_freed == 4
set booth_g_plays = 5
elif flag.revelers_freed == 5
set booth_g_plays = 6
elif flag.revelers_freed == 6
set booth_g_plays = 7
elif flag.revelers_freed == 7
set booth_g_plays = 8
elif flag.revelers_freed == 8
set booth_g_plays = 9
elif flag.revelers_freed == 9
set booth_g_plays = 10
elif flag.revelers_freed == 10
set booth_g_plays = 11
elif flag.revelers_freed == 11
set booth_g_plays = 12
elif flag.revelers_freed == 12
set booth_g_plays = 13
endif
set found_flag
Narrator: Tiny tin footlights flare along the miniature stage, and red silk ribbons spill from the rafters like cartoon blood as the wooden figures jerk into motion.
if flag.raum_slain
-> g_raum
elif flag.vessla_slain
-> g_vessla
else
-> g_generic
endif

~ g_raum
set fd_fallen_harvest
Narrator: A ragged scarecrow puppet with a carved crow's beak rattles across the boards, shedding tufts of straw and loops of crimson ribbon as four tiny hero dolls whack it flat.
fd_host_puppets [smile]: Behold the terror of the cornfield, snipped and stuffed and tumbled into the chaff. Tell me, brave ones, what did you make of the strings?
* [Arcana DC 20] Name the trick behind the puppet -> g_win | g_lose
* Tell the puppeteer something true about that fight -> g_share

~ g_vessla
set fd_fallen_vessla
Narrator: A crooked-house witch in a tall pointed hat capers across the stage, until four button-eyed hero puppets topple her into a laughable heap of red satin streamers.
fd_host_puppets [smile]: Down goes the old crone of the eaves, all spools and splinters now. Tell me, sharpest eyes, how does the little show hold together?
* [Arcana DC 20] Name the trick behind the puppet -> g_win | g_lose
* Tell the puppeteer something true about that fight -> g_share

~ g_generic
Narrator: A faceless shadow cut from black felt looms over a doll in a hero's tin hat, before bursting apart into harmless curls of scarlet ribbon.
fd_host_puppets [smile]: Look how the great dark pops like a paper bag when the heroes swing their sticks. Now then, what secret hides behind my velvet valence?
* [Arcana DC 20] Name the trick behind the puppet -> g_win | g_lose
* Tell the puppeteer something true about that fight -> g_share

~ g_share
approve rook_coldwake +2 tobin_hayward +2 delphine_ravelle +1: You spoke the plain truth about the dread of that real fight
Narrator: {name} speaks plainly of the cold dread and the cost of that real night, and for a breath the red ribbon puppets hang dead still against the painted sky.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Look at that, darlings, one honest line and the whole cheap curtain goes quiet.
check Arcana DC 15 -> g_win | g_lose

~ g_win
set fool_tickets += 3
fd_host_puppets [weary]: Ah, you see right through the varnish to the knot beneath. Take your three tickets before you spoil the comedy for the whole row.
-> g_start

~ g_lose
fd_host_puppets [smile]: Pretty words, my dears, though far too heavy for a puppet booth. The ribbons dance on, and my tickets stay on the hook.
-> g_start
